{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>My bow in my hand — it replays:</b> Some say: the meaning is אחליפנה (I would exchange it) from hand to hand, and it would not depart from me. Some say: תחלוף, like כל בני חלוף (all children of exchange) — I would shoot arrows from it and not miss. Others say: that I would exchange the bow in my hand and had no need for another. Some say: בידי תחליף — and it would not be cut off by the strength of my hand."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:03:56.076984057Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}